	(gr_text "FABRICATION\nJLCPCB 4 layers, 1.6 mm, stackup JLC04161H-7628, 1 oz outer / 0.5 oz inner, ENIG. Board 70 x 109.2 mm.\nVias tented on both sides. The exposed-pad vias of IC4, IC8, IC9 and IC15 are open on the top only, through their pads;\nIC4's 4 sit in the gaps of its paste grid. Everything is tented on the bottom (IC8/IC9 sit above the PoE module IC5).\nImpedance control +-10 %: L1/L4 100 ohm differential, 0.21 mm / 0.19 mm gap (Ethernet TRD*, CSI DPHY0_*, DPHY1_*);\nL1/L4 90 ohm differential, 0.24 mm / 0.15 mm gap (USB2_*, RP2354A USB_D*). Min track 0.1 mm, min clearance 0.1 mm,\nmin via 0.45/0.2 mm. J2 sits 0.3 mm from the edge and the USB-C J8 shell is flush with it: no V-score there.\n\nASSEMBLY\nAll parts except IC5 are on the top: reflow the top side only.\nIC5 (Ag59824-LPB, bottom side) by hand (iron / hot air); it never goes through reflow hanging upside down.\nHot air profile: peak 230-245 C, 30-90 s above 217 C, soak 150-180 C 30-90 s, ramp up <= 3 C/s, down <= 6 C/s.\nThrough-hole parts by hand: IC3 (MagJack), J6 / J14 (XT60), J7, J9, J13, C20, and J8's 4 USB-C shell tabs.\nL1: dot = pad 1 (+1V1). IC12 (SHT45) and the other symmetric parts: pin 1 at the silk dot.\nCM5: M2.5 screws from below (head <= 4.5 mm), nuts on the CM5 side. Mounting holes H1-H4: M2.\nH3 lies inside the PoE input lines: nylon M2 screw and nylon standoff there (isolation).\n\nTEST\nPoE isolation: 1500 V 10/700 us impulse test only, at normal air pressure. No 1500 Vrms or 2250 Vdc hipot\n(Y-caps C21/C24 and the module are not rated for it). Then >= 2 MOhm at 500 Vdc, primary to GND."
		(at 175 50 0)
		(layer "Cmts.User")
		(uuid "f9112a5c-1237-4d30-a26e-ea5fb9fd0135")
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
				(thickness 0.15)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
	)
